    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1718094227094032.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2024-06-05-2024-06-05-0179",
    "chunk_index": 179,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "9124bdb525f3d21d337de50d93051c83",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1862,
    "chunk_text": "As a student who came from the rural areas and also who had had the opportunity of receiving admission to a popular school in Colombo, the Royal College, through the government scholarship scheme, I am one who will always attest about the gap and the seriousness of this gap between the rural schools and the city schools or the prominent schools in the country. Therefore, it is important that we pay our attention to this area.\n\nIn this regard, Sir, I would like to table* a letter from a particular charity based in Australia, who have been doing wonderful work in Sri Lanka from 2004 onwards.\n\nteam will arrive here in Sri Lanka and they are due to train even teachers from the Central Province. It was at my request that they have moved to the Central Province, but there is a difficulty. I was able to connect them with the Governor of the Eastern Province, Mr. Senthil Thondaman, and he was good enough to instruct the Provincial Director of Education to incorporate that programme in an official manner. But, unfortunately, the provincial educational authorities of the Central Province still have not got involved properly with that programme. Therefore, I am requesting the Hon. Minister to go through the letter which I have tabled and which had been handed over to Ms. Wasantha Perera, former Secretary, and instruct the current Secretary on further action. Unfortunately, Secretaries to Ministries are changing like in \"Musical Chairs\"; every Secretary coming to the Ministry of Education does not last beyond a year. Therefore, I would prefer if the Minister takes it upon himself to instruct the current Secretary to have a discussion with the National Institute of Education, incorporate it into our National Education Policy Framework and see that this programme is implemented for the benefit of all our children studying in government schools."
  },
