    "chunk_size_bytes": 947,
    "chunk_text": "So, I think this balance needs to be understood; for sure, it needs to be understood and needs to be upheld. We must not go on undermining it in anyway. Therefore, it is pertinent for us to remind ourselves that we have a responsibility. We look to the Supreme Court to get the constitutionality of issues properly considered and determined. That is what it is there for and that role cannot be taken over by the Legislature. There is separation of powers and we must maintain that. So, it is really worrying that the President said that. We know that there are the concepts of Parliamentary supremacy and constitutional supremacy.\n\nUnfortunately, Sri Lanka does not have post-enactment judicial review. The President, the other day, referred to the process of creating the 1978 Constitution and said that two Hon. Members who are in this House\n\n1365 1366\n\n[\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0daf\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dca \u0dd2\u0dc3\u200d\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dca\u0dad\u0db1 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2024 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0db1\u0dd2 20"
