    "description": "Hansard of June 20, 2024",
    "url_metadata": "https://www.parliament.lk/en/business-of-parliament/hansards",
    "lang": "si-ta-en",
    "url_pdf": "https://www.parliament.lk/uploads/documents/hansard/1720176847036370.pdf",
    "chunk_id": "2024-06-20-2024-06-20-0142",
    "chunk_index": 142,
    "language": "si-ta-en",
    "md5": "6070de1ebec08f2b3030f7119eb8bf6c",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 2245,
    "chunk_text": "Unfortunately, Sri Lanka does not have post-enactment judicial review. The President, the other day, referred to the process of creating the 1978 Constitution and said that two Hon. Members who are in this House\n\n1365 1366\n\n[\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0daf\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dca \u0dd2\u0dc3\u200d\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dca\u0dad\u0db1 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dad\u0dcf]\n\n2024 \u0da2\u0dd6\u0db1\u0dd2 20\n\nIn addition to that, there is also the breach of the social contract people have made, surrendering their power to Parliament and the Judiciary to act on their behalf. Human morality was shaped in the course evolution over millions of years, dealing with social and ethical dilemmas which cropped up in the lives of the hunters and gatherers. Most of the injustices in the contemporary world result from large-scale structural biases rather than individual prejudices. But, the hunter-gatherer brain did not evolve to detect those structural biases.\n\nJudgments could be wrong and be biased, but maintaining the structural safeguards such as separation of powers among the Executive, Judiciary and the Legislature is paramount rather than thinking of individuals. Then, what should we do? Should we adopt the liberal dogma and trust the aggregate of individual voters, that voters would decide everything and reduce the justice system to majoritarianism? What kind of nonsense and crap is that? Then, you do not need the Judiciary and we can vote on everything in Parliament.\n\nWe now face global problems without having a global community. Neither the Facebook, nationalism nor religion is near creating a global community anywhere. That is the truth. The human quest to understand the truth and find justice has been failed. If you are in government and take the view that Parliamentary supremacy supersedes judicial supremacy, we are bound to fail, as we have already seen.\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dca\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0db8\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) Hon. Member, your time is over. \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0d89\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0db8\u0dbb\u0dad\u0dca\u0db1 \u0db8\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b87\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bae\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba9) (The Hon. Eran Wickramaratne) I am concluding, Sir."
  },
