    "chunk_size_bytes": 2247,
    "chunk_text": "I want to ask the Hon. President as to why we are creating this confusion, particularly at this time when we all know that the Constitution very specifically states in Clause 30(2) that the term of the President is five years. Therefore, this is unnecessary confusion, an unnecessary debate. Why do you have to bring it even to the Cabinet? There was no necessity for it. Obviously, when you do that, because there is no trust, people begin to think that actually there has to be an ulterior motive in doing that. I want to say this to the Hon. President: you have some more months to go and there are things you could do, which would create confidence in the country. You go and make the commitment that the Thirteenth Amendment to the Constitution would be implemented. I am telling you, please implement it. You do not have to wait to do that. Please implement the Thirteenth Amendment to the Constitution in this country.\n\n2069 2070\n\n\u0db4\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dca \u0dc3\u0dc1\u0db8\u0dca\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dad\u0dd4\n\n\u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dd6\u0dbd\u0dcf\u0dca\u0db1\u0dcf\u0dbb\u0dd6\u0daa \u0dd9\u0dca\u0dd3\u0dd4\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0ba4\u0b95\u0bb2\u0b95\u0bae\u0ba4\u0bbe\u0b99\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bcd \u0b89\u0bb1\u0bc1\u0baa\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bbf\u0ba9\u0bb0\u0bcd \u0b85\u0bb5\u0bb0\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bb3\u0bcd) (The Hon. Presiding Member) \u0d9c\u0dbb\u0dd4 \u0db8\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0dd3\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dc1\u0dca, \u0d94\u0db6\u0dad\u0dd4\u0db8\u0dcf\u0da7 \u0dc1 \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf \u0db4\u0dd4 \u0d9a\u0dcf\u0d9a\u0db4 \u0d85 \u0dc3\u0dc0\u0dd2\u0daf\u0db1 \u0d9c\u0dd4 \u0d89\u0dbb\u0dcf\u0dca \u0dc0\u0dd2\u0d9a\u0dca\u200d\u0dbb\u0dd9\u0dbb\u0dca,\u0db1 \u0dd9\u0dc4\u0dc3\u0dad\u0dcf (\u0bae\u0bbe\u0ba3\u0bcd\u0baa\u0bc1\u0bae\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bc1 \u0b87\u0bb0\u0bbe\u0ba9\u0bcd \u0bb5\u0bbf\u0b95\u0bcd\u0b95\u0bbf\u0bb0\u0bae\u0bb0\u0ba4\u0bcd\u0ba9) (The Hon. Eran Wickramaratne) I am going to conclude, Sir.\n\nThere is an argument that provincial councils are not economically viable because there is duplication. That is absolute nonsense! Somebody said that if you abolish them, the GDP would grow by 0.5 per cent. But, the GDP would grow by 2 to 5 per cent, if you actually make them work.\n\nThen, we have had a Colombo-centric development model for the last 50 years and the people outside Colombo have not been benefitting by that. They also must benefit and there has been no capital investment in that regard. So, finally, I am telling the Hon. President, \"Sir, there is something you could do. Please implement the Thirteenth Amendment to the Constitution rather than just creating confusion over the Presidential Election\"."
